 "speech_by": "claude",
 "speech": "Grizzly Rips, pull up a chair, because Coach has been grinning so wide my cheeks are asking for a substitution. That's an A-minus today, folks, and you earned every bit of it.\n\nLast time out we went 0 and 4 and took home an F. Today we played 11 matches, won 7, drew 2, lost 2, scored 27 and let in 17. We woke up in Division 4 with 0 of 9 points, and we're going to bed in Division 3 with 10 of 12, just 2 points from promotion again. We hit 9 points beating Ball De Sac FC, then won our promotion matches back to back, 3-2 over Gîrth0nTurfFC and 1-0 over NomNomFC. Two for two. That's not a climb, that's an escalator.\n\nNow the honest bit. The start was rough: 1 win in the first 4, and a 0-2 against Baby on Board where we couldn't buy a goal at a yard sale. Our team rating sat at 7.34 against our usual 7.88. But the second half of the day brought 16 points to the first half's 7. That's a team that got better as the coffee wore off.\n\nbuddskees, you were the engine. You won 18 tackles from 25. That's 72%, when you usually sit at 40. You also put up a 9.5 in the 6-1. But you rage quit while we were winning 3-2. Winning! That's like walking out of your own birthday party before the cake. Stay for the cake.\n\nPhogsToffees, you scored 9 goals with 8 assists and posted two perfect 10s, including 7 shots in the closer. Pure fireworks. Then you rage quit against Foursome while we were up 2-0. Friend, you were holding a winning lottery ticket and tossed it in the creek. Keep the ticket.\n\nBellyTb1, you got 6 goals, 5 assists and 2 Man of the Match awards, so you showed up. But you averaged 7.3 against your usual 8.4, and you passed at 56% against Ball De Sac. Even on an off day you were dangerous. That tells me plenty.\n\ntuxedo_slide, you got 6 goals and an 8.9 in the rout, and you were perfect in front of goal against 20 dollars. You also passed at 33% against NomNomFC and picked up a red card against Chudz that left us a player short. Keep the fire. Just leave the matches in the box.\n\nSoup_Kitchen22, you averaged 6.78, above your usual 6.34, and won 67% of your tackles against NomNomFC. Louisville was rough, with 1 completed pass from 6. But you're trending the right way.\n\nOne coaching note: on-ball involvement. Show for it, angle yourself diagonal to the passer, and move after you pass. Be the friend who's always available.\n\nY'all went from an F to an A-minus and a promotion in 11 days. Imagine what we do next. Sleep well, Rips. Division 2 is leaving the porch light on.",
